      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('我们先看真实轨迹，没有停在最后的 0 分：15 步版本里，模型反复执行 next（下一页）和 back（返回），一直没有进入 buy（购买）。所以当时最自然的怀疑是：会不会只是 15 步太短，还没来得及做完？', 'We inspected the actual traces before interpreting the zero reward. At 15 steps the model repeatedly used next and back and never reached a buy transition. The natural hypothesis was therefore that 15 steps might simply be too short to finish.')}</p>
      <div class="before-after horizon-compare">
        <div class="before"><span>15 步</span><strong>next ↔ back ↔ next …</strong><p>{t('几个导航动作反复出现；轨迹走满 15 步，仍没有进入购买动作，任务得分为 0。', 'A few navigation actions repeat; the trace reaches the 15-step limit without a buy action, and the task score is zero.')}</p></div>
        <div class="after"><span>30 步</span><strong>{t('多出来的 15 步没有打开新路径', 'The extra 15 steps do not open a new path')}</strong><p>{t('模型仍在同样几个导航动作里打转，没有进入 buy；15 步和 30 步两种条件的任务得分都为 0。', 'The model keeps cycling through the same navigation actions and still never reaches buy; both the 15-step and 30-step conditions score zero.')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <ol class="horizon-decision">
        <li><span>01</span><strong>{t('先不在 prompt 里硬禁 next / back', 'Do not hard-ban next / back in the prompt first')}</strong><p>{t('硬禁会同时改变提示词和动作选择规则，分不清问题到底是步数不够，还是我们把行为教偏了。', 'A hard ban would change both the prompt and the action rule, making it unclear whether the issue was short horizon or an artificial steering effect.')}</p></li>
        <li><span>02</span><strong>{t('采用第二种方案：保持原 prompt，只把 15 步改成 30 步', 'Use the second plan: keep the prompt fixed and change only 15 steps to 30')}</strong><p>{t('这样只测试“多给时间有没有用”，不把 prompt 干预混进同一个实验。', 'This isolates whether extra time helps without mixing a prompt intervention into the same test.')}</p></li>
        <li><span>03</span><strong>{t('结果仍然打转，于是回到接口语义', 'The loop remained, so we moved back to action-interface semantics')}</strong><p>{t('步数解释被排除；后续继续检查 prompt、deliberation 和 action channel，但不能把这一步说成已经解决最终低分。', 'Horizon is not the main explanation; later work investigates prompt, deliberation, and the action channel, but this step does not solve the final low score.')}</p></li>
      </ol>
