  <section id="mechanism" class="briefing-slide tone-gold" aria-labelledby="mechanism-title">
    <div class="slide-inner taskvector-slide taskvector-method-slide">
      <h2 id="mechanism-title">{t('参数更新开始发生后，我们开始追它往哪里学', 'After parameter updates began, we traced where they moved')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('TaskVector 把一次训练前后的参数差记成一个方向。我们先问三个小问题：参数移动了多少、连续更新方向是否接近、这个方向被拿掉以后行为会不会跟着变。', 'TaskVector records the parameter difference before and after one training step as a direction. We ask three small questions first: how far the parameters moved, whether consecutive updates point similarly, and whether behavior changes when that direction is removed.')}</p>
      <div class="taskvector-equation" aria-label={t('TaskVector 定义', 'TaskVector definition')}>
        <span>TaskVector</span>
        <strong>v = θ<sub>after</sub> − θ<sub>before</sub></strong>
        <p>{t('θ 表示模型参数；v 表示一次学习让参数真正移动的方向。', 'θ denotes model parameters; v is the direction that one learning step actually moves them.')}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="taskvector-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><strong>{t('看长度', 'measure magnitude')}</strong><p>{t('‖v‖ 告诉我们参数移动了多少。', '‖v‖ tells us how much the parameters moved.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><strong>{t('看方向', 'compare direction')}</strong><p>{t('比较相邻 TaskVector 的夹角 / cosine，看连续更新是否朝相近方向。', 'Compare angles / cosine between successive TaskVectors to see whether updates point similarly.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><strong>{t('做干预', 'test by intervention')}</strong><p>{t('拿掉累计 SD-LoRA 参数变化，再看同一批输入的动作选择是否改变。', 'Remove the accumulated SD-LoRA parameter change and test whether actions change on the same inputs.')}</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="taskvector-paper"><strong>{t('参考思想', 'Reference idea')}</strong><a href={taskArithmeticHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ilharco et al. · Editing Models with Task Arithmetic ↗</a><span>{t('论文把微调前后的参数差看成权重空间方向；我们进一步追踪 OpenEVO 连续自我训练产生的一系列方向。', 'The paper treats the before-after fine-tuning difference as a direction in weight space; we extend that idea to a sequence of OpenEVO self-training updates.')}</span></p>
      <p class="slide-bridge">{t('这一页定义怎么观察参数；下一页展示这个观察带来的两个直接证据。', 'This slide defines how we inspect parameters; the next slide shows two direct pieces of evidence from that inspection.')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('TaskVector 完整推导与实验门槛', 'Full TaskVector derivation and experimental thresholds')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">14 / 23</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="taskvector-behavior" class="briefing-slide tone-gold" aria-labelledby="taskvector-behavior-title">
    <div class="slide-inner taskvector-behavior-slide">
      <h2 id="taskvector-behavior-title">{t('拿掉累计参数变化后，24 个输入全部换了第一选择', 'After removing the accumulated parameter change, all 24 inputs changed their top choice')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('1.7B 的 7 次正式更新没有从头到尾稳定同向。前半段像在试路；最近一次和前一次很一致。随后我们做了一个直接干预：把累计 SD-LoRA 参数变化拿掉，再让模型看同一批输入。', 'The seven formal 1.7B updates were not aligned from start to finish. The early segment looks exploratory; the latest admitted update aligns strongly with the previous one. We then ran a direct intervention: remove the accumulated SD-LoRA parameter change and ask the model to process the same inputs again.')}</p>
      <div class="taskvector-behavior-grid">
        <article><span>{t('相邻方向相似度', 'adjacent direction similarity')}</span><strong>0.56 → 0.35 → 0.03 → -0.02 → 0.11 → 0.79</strong><p>{t('前几次更新方向不稳定；最后一次和前一次明显接近，说明后期可能开始沿着更稳定的参数方向移动。', 'Early update directions are unstable; the latest step is clearly close to the previous one, suggesting a more stable parameter direction may be emerging.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>{t('行为干预', 'behavior intervention')}</span><strong>24 / 24</strong><p>{t('拿掉累计 SD-LoRA 参数变化以后，固定 24 个输入的第一选择全部翻转。', 'After removing the accumulated SD-LoRA parameter change, the top choice flipped on all 24 fixed inputs.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>{t('目标拟合', 'target fit')}</span><strong>0.15 → 1.02</strong><p>{t('模型对原本目标行为的拟合 loss 明显变差，说明这组参数变化已经进入决策过程。', 'Fit loss on the original target behavior became much worse, showing that this parameter change is already active in the decision process.')}</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="taskvector-behavior-boundary"><strong>{t('这一步说明什么', 'What this establishes')}</strong>{t('TaskVector 已经能改变模型行为；下一步要继续区分哪些方向带来真正任务能力，哪些方向只是改变了动作偏好。最终 WebShop 分数仍由冻结终评回答。', 'TaskVector already changes model behavior. The next question is which directions contribute real task ability and which only change action preference. The frozen final evaluation still answers the final WebShop score.')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={measurementPackHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><ExternalBrandMark href={measurementPackHref} /> PR #317 · {t('参数机制分析', 'parameter-mechanism analysis')}</a> · <a href={technicalHref}>{t('完整 Gram matrix 与 Frobenius 几何', 'Full Gram matrix and Frobenius geometry')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">15 / 23</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="gdr" class="briefing-slide tone-rose" aria-labelledby="gdr-title">
    <div class="slide-inner">
      <h2 id="gdr-title">{t('GDR 把一次参数更新变成可测的准入判断', 'GDR turns one parameter update into a measurable admission decision')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('GDR = Gated Delta Rule。论文里的 Gated Delta Rule 用 S / k / v 描述快速记忆更新：S 是当前 fast-memory state，k 是要改写的关联位置，v 是准备写入的新 value。OpenEVO 的可执行实验没有把 SD-LoRA 直接代入这个公式；我们把这个思想落成了更保守的 gate。', 'GDR = Gated Delta Rule. In the paper, Gated Delta Rule uses S / k / v to describe a fast-memory update: S is the current fast-memory state, k is the association address to rewrite, and v is the new value to write. The executed OpenEVO experiment did not plug SD-LoRA directly into that equation; we implemented the idea as a more conservative gate.')}</p>
      <div class="gdr-paper-map" aria-label={t('Gated Delta Rule 论文里的变量', 'Variables in the Gated Delta Rule paper')}>
        <div><span>S</span><strong>{t('当前 fast-memory state', 'current fast-memory state')}</strong></div>
        <div><span>k</span><strong>{t('要改写的关联位置', 'association address')}</strong></div>
        <div><span>v</span><strong>{t('准备写入的新 value', 'new value to write')}</strong></div>
        <p>{t('公式直觉是沿 k 修正旧关联，再把 v 写入状态；gating 控制这次写入有多强。', 'The equation corrects the old association along k, writes v into the state, and uses gating to control write strength.')}</p>
        <a href={gatedDeltaPaperHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Yang et al. · Gated Delta Networks ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="before-after gdr-flow">
        <div class="before"><span>{t('论文给我们的启发', 'paper inspiration')}</span><strong>{t('修正旧关联，再写入新信息', 'correct the old association, then write the new information')}</strong><p>{t('这个思想解释了为什么我们一开始会把 GDR 看成一种“擦掉旧方向、写入新方向”的参数更新思路。', 'This idea explains why we initially treated GDR as a parameter-update idea that removes an old direction and writes a new one.')}</p></div>
        <div class="after"><span>{t('我们真正跑的 GDR-v1', 'our executed GDR-v1')}</span><strong>{t('当前 OpenEVO 状态 + 完整候选状态 → 16-task probe → 是否采用', 'current OpenEVO state plus full candidate state → 16-task probe → admission decision')}</strong><p>{t('这里的 state 是整套 OpenEVO 运行状态和候选运行状态；v / k 没有直接映射成某个 SD-LoRA 张量。gate 用短期任务表现判断候选是否进入下一轮。', 'Here, state means the full OpenEVO running state and the candidate running state; v / k are not directly mapped to a specific SD-LoRA tensor. The gate uses short-horizon task behavior to decide whether the candidate enters the next round.')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="gdr-why-gate"><strong>{t('为什么采用 gate 版本？', 'Why use a gate version?')}</strong>{t('当时还不能可靠判断哪段参数该擦、擦多少、哪段方向更正确，所以先使用可测任务表现作保守替代：候选先训练，再由 probe 决定是否进入下一轮。这个选择产生新的科学问题：短期不退步的准入，会不会提前截断长期有价值的更新？', 'At that point we could not reliably identify which parameter segment should be removed, how much to remove, or which new direction was correct. We therefore used measurable task behavior as a conservative substitute: train the candidate, then let the probe decide whether it enters the next round. This creates a new scientific question: can a short-horizon non-regression gate cut off updates that would become valuable later?')}</p>
      <p class="bottom-claim">{t('因此我们把两个计数分开看：OpenEVO 训练出了多少个 SD-LoRA 候选，以及 GDR 最终让多少个候选真正更新到后续模型。下一页就是 1.7B 正式线的实际结果。', 'We therefore track two counts separately: how many SD-LoRA candidates OpenEVO trained, and how many GDR allowed to update later model states. The next slide shows the formal 1.7B result.')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('GDR 的完整判定逻辑与实验定义', 'Full GDR decision logic and experiment definition')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">16 / 23</p>
    </div>
  </section>
